        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d664e69a-f9b5-5748-99ae-8d59b3565259",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Lüliang, Shanxi, Shaanxi, Yellow River, Jinzhong, Taiyuan, Linfen, Xinzhou, Fuxin, Liaoning, Zhongyang County, China\n- Organizations: Liaoning Technical University, State Administration of Work Safety\n- Topics: population, administration, geography, census\n\nFacts:\n- Lüliang is a prefecture-level city in western Shanxi province, China.\n- Lüliang borders Shaanxi across the Yellow River to the west, Jinzhong and Taiyuan to the east, Linfen to the south, and Xinzhou to the north.\n- Lüliang has a total area of 21,143 km2 and a total population of 3,727,057.\n- At the 2010 census, the metro area of Lüliang had a population of 320,142.\n- At the 2010 census, the prefecture of Fuxin had a total population of 1,819,339.\n- At the 2010 census, 669,317 people in Fuxin lived in the built-up area comprising four urban districts collectively known as Fuxin City.\n- Zhongyang County is under the administration of Lüliang city.\n- Liaoning Technical University is located in Fuxin, Liaoning, China.\n- Liaoning Technical University is also known as LNTU and Liaoning University of Engineering and Technology.\n- Liaoning Technical University is administered by the Liaoning provincial government and the State Administration of Work Safety.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
